[seller.step] write · agent (claude-haiku-5-5): Packaged LibreOffice headless as a stdlib-only converter at /opt/tool/convert.py. It validates the input (extension, size, zip or RTF structure), copies it into a private temp directory, and converts with a per-run LibreOffice profile so concurrent runs do not collide. It exports PDF/A-2b via the calc, writer, and impress PDF filters, writes <outdir>/<stem>.pdf, and prints the absolute path last. Exit codes: 2 for bad extension, unreadable or corrupt input, or conversion failure; 3 for inputs over 25 MB; 4 for the 60 s timeout, which kills the whole process group. tests/make_fixtures.py builds docx, odt, rtf, pptx and xlsx samples with the standard library, and tests/test_convert.py covers formats, PDF/A markers, text extraction, every xlsx sheet, title metadata with stem fallback, non-ASCII names, exit codes, timeout, and concurrency. Caveats: I could not execute anything in this session, so the tests are unrun. The PDF/A and title checks depend on LibreOffice's XMP and Info output, and the title fallback to the file stem relies on LibreOffice's default behaviour. The pptx fixture is hand-written and may need adjustment. Run `cd /opt/tool && python3 -m pytest -q` to verify.
