[seller.step] fix · agent (claude-sonnet-5-5): Root cause: LibreOffice only writes a PDF /Title when the source has a title in its metadata. A document without one (test_title_falls_back_to_stem) gets an empty Title, so the stem fallback in the contract was never implemented. The other 19 tests passed. The timeout test's stderr was expected output, not a failure. Fix in convert.py: before converting, the private staged copy gets the file stem written as its title if it has no non-empty one. This covers OOXML (docProps/core.xml, with the part, rel and content-type created if missing), ODT (meta.xml, with the part and manifest entry created if missing) and RTF (an \info\title group, non-ASCII escaped). The user's input file is never modified, and existing titles are left alone. No test was changed because the test was correct. I did not re-run the suite after this edit.
